 "notes": [
  "The text says 100 ohm resistors, but the schematic label says 10k; I used 100 ohm as the text and parts list do.",
  "The parts list says 10 hook-up wires, but the circuit image shows only 4 jumper wires: GND and pins 8, 7 and 6. I modelled those 4. The speaker leads are the speaker's own wires.",
  "The catalogue names the breadboard halves 't' (rows a-e) and 'b' (rows f-j). In the image the top half is labelled f-j and the bottom half a-e. I mapped the top half to bank 'b' and the bottom half to bank 't'. The resistors straddle the centre gap.",
  "The black wire goes to the Arduino GND pin beside AREF. I assumed that is GND.2; the catalogue does not say which of its GND ports it is.",
  "Speaker polarity is assumed: port 1 is the black lead, which goes to the ground rail. Port 2 is the red lead, which goes to the resistor column. The speaker's ports are symmetric in practice.",
  "The ground rail is the top negative rail 'tn'. Exact hole numbers on the rail are approximate; every hole in a rail is the same strip.",
  "Pin 8 goes to speaker 1, pin 7 to speaker 2 and pin 6 to speaker 3, matching the sketch comment."
 ],
